// logic.memql -- harness namespace (#586).
//
// Logic body for the memory-consolidation automation
// (dsl/harness/automations.memql).
//
// Why the heavy loop lives Go-side (the same split the knowledge
// refresh-cron and planner budget automations made): consolidation
// needs (a) per-owner iteration, (b) similarity CLUSTERING of the
// episode batch, (c) a blocking LLM distill call per cluster, (d)
// similarTo dedup + the confidence bump / decay ARITHMETIC, and (e)
// max(createdAt) over the batch to advance the watermark. The MemQL
// parser has no arithmetic on number / datetime fields and no
// in-DSL clustering primitive, so the precise math + the iteration
// run in Go (the harness consolidation handler, registered by the
// agent-node init path), where they are cheap. The DSL body is the
// scheduled ENTRY POINT; everything downstream of "a run fired" is
// Go-side.
//
// The Go handler's contract (so the loop is fully specified even
// though it is not expressible in the DSL today):
//
//   for each owner with episodic activity since their watermark:
//     1. cursor  := read v1:harness:consolidationCursor for owner
//                   (watermark defaults to epoch on first run)
//     2. batch   := episodic nodes (observation / step / plan) with
//                   createdAt > cursor.watermark, capped at
//                   MEMQL_HARNESS_CONSOLIDATION_BATCH_MAX (bounded cost)
//     3. clusters := group batch by embedding similarity
//     4. for each cluster:
//          belief := ai("consolidateMemory", {episodes: cluster, ...})
//          if belief.distilled == false: continue   // nothing stable
//          match := similarTo({ text: belief.content,
//                               concept: "v1:harness:semanticMemory",
//                               limit: 1 })           // active only
//          if match.cosine >= MEMQL_HARNESS_CONSOLIDATION_DEDUP_THRESHOLD:
//              reinforceHarnessSemanticMemory({       // no duplicate
//                memoryId: match.id,
//                confidence: bump(match.confidence),  // Go arithmetic
//                reinforceCount: match.reinforceCount + 1,
//                sourceEpisodes: dedupMerge(match.sourceEpisodes,
//                                           cluster.ids) })
//          else:
//              createHarnessSemanticMemory({          // new belief
//                kind: belief.kind, content: belief.content,
//                sourceEpisodes: cluster.ids,
//                confidence: belief.confidence })
//     5. decay sweep: for each active belief unreinforced past
//        MEMQL_HARNESS_CONSOLIDATION_DECAY_DAYS:
//          decayHarnessSemanticMemory({ memoryId, confidence: decay(...) })
//          if decayed < MEMQL_HARNESS_CONSOLIDATION_PRUNE_CONFIDENCE:
//              pruneHarnessSemanticMemory({ memoryId })
//     6. advanceHarnessConsolidationCursor({
//          watermark: max(createdAt over batch),
//          episodesSeen: cursor.episodesSeen + batch.len })
//
// The bump / decay / dedup-merge helpers are pure functions, unit-
// tested in component/memql/harness_consolidation_test.go so the
// decisions (when to reinforce vs. create, how confidence moves, when
// to prune) are covered without a DB; the scheduled + LLM-distill path
// is integration-covered. Steps 4's reinforce-vs-create branch is the
// acceptance criterion "re-running reinforces rather than duplicates";
// step 6 is "consolidation is incremental (watermark respected)".

@description("Entry point for the daily memory-consolidation automation (#586). Per #586 the precise per-owner loop -- similarity clustering of the since-watermark episode batch, the blocking LLM distill per cluster, similarTo dedup, the confidence bump / decay arithmetic, and the max(createdAt) watermark advance -- runs in the Go harness consolidation handler (the same DSL-entry / Go-loop split the knowledge refresh-cron made), because the MemQL parser has neither arithmetic on number/datetime fields nor an in-DSL clustering primitive. This body is the scheduled trigger surface; the file header documents the full Go-handler contract it drives. Returns a sentinel until the handler is wired (mirrors logicRefreshDueKnowledgeDomains).")
logic consolidateMemory {
  args {
    event object @required
  }
  body {
    // Phase scaffolding: the per-owner consolidation loop (read since
    // watermark -> cluster -> LLM distill -> similarTo dedup ->
    // reinforce/create -> decay/prune -> advance watermark) is owned
    // by the Go harness consolidation handler. The full contract is in
    // this file's header; the mutations it calls
    // (createHarnessSemanticMemory / reinforceHarnessSemanticMemory /
    // decayHarnessSemanticMemory / pruneHarnessSemanticMemory /
    // advanceHarnessConsolidationCursor) ship in
    // dsl/harness/mutations.memql and the distill prompt
    // (consolidateMemory) in dsl/harness/prompts.memql.
    return args.event.topic
  }
}
